% A caveat is advisory by default and fatal under strict. One switch between
% "best effort, and I know what I signed up for" and "only what is exactly
% equivalent".

### name: strict.off.division-is-translated
--- note
MariaDB's DECIMAL division adds four fractional digits where SEL's adds ten.
Verified on 11.8: SELECT 1/3 is 0.3333 and SEL says 0.3333333333.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
1 / 3
--- expect
(1 / 3)
===
### name: strict.on.division-is-refused
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
1 / 3
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:3
===
### name: strict.on.upper-is-refused
--- note
UPPER is ASCII-only in SEL and Unicode-aware in MariaDB.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
UPPER("a")
--- error
E_SQL_UNSUPPORTED 1:1
===
### name: strict.on.exact-functions-still-translate
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
TRIM("  x  ")
--- expect
REGEXP_REPLACE('  x  ', '^[ \\t\\r\\n]+|[ \\t\\r\\n]+$', '')
===
### name: strict.on.comparison-is-exact
--- dialect
mariadb
--- options
{"strict": true}
--- source
1 < 2
--- expect
(1 < 2)
